# Business-impact reports are client-account assets — generated, not tracked.
# `report_sink` in .assert-iq/config.yaml writes them under reports/.
# baseline.json IS tracked: it is the team's pre-QI reference data.
#
# IMPORTANT — additive patterns only, never negations (`!pattern`).
# A .gitignore deeper in the tree outranks .git/info/exclude, so a negation
# here silently RE-INCLUDES the file and defeats a trial-mode install. This
# file previously used `*.html` / `*.json` plus `!baseline.json` /
# `!.gitignore`, which is exactly why those two showed up in `git status`
# after `--mode=trial`.
# Enforced by unit-gitignore-hygiene.sh.
reports/
